      "text": "WHAT? WHY?",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 7,
      "bbox": [
        604,
        194,
        699,
        915
      ],
      "margin_number": 147,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Observe that τί, which you have learnt to mean ‘what?’ can also, and very commonly, mean ‘why?’ When τί does mean ‘why?’, it is in the acc. case and being used adverbially. Its literal meaning is ‘in relation to what?’ or ‘in respect of what?’ – in other words, ‘why?’",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": 147,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "order": 8,
      "bbox": [
        712,
        194,
        731,
        368
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "INDIRECT SPEECH",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
